From 9caa54ba2a61708827fd7b58708b9299f3932d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:24:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(motion): Circular climbs to clearance between its
 rings

A Circular with several rings ran each ring through its own level
ladder. The next ring's first descent left the last ring's floor with
one diagonal rapid up to clearance, across the core still to cut, and
verification held the post (rapid move N travels through stock). The
vault had the same link.

Each ring after the first now starts with a straight climb to
clearance at the last ring's end, so its entry traverses over the
stock. Two goldens gain that one move. The unit tests move to
circular_tests.rs to keep the file under 400 lines.

The helix entry still touches the last ring's helix at the same depth
(the crossing law): #3109.

Fixes #2898

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
